<spell-notebook "transition theming">
	<header level="1">
		Transition
		<header>A transition is an animation used to show or hide content, or to draw attention to it.</>
	</>
	<transition-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			A transition draws nothing of its own: the animations are the foundation's `animations.css`
			catalogue, shared by every component. The `pulsating` ring reads `--ui-transition-inverted-pulse` when `inverted`
			(set it on the element, an ancestor or `:root`), and `color` tints it. Style the animated
			box through `::part(transition)`. Never set the `--_*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-transition::part(transition) {
			  border-radius: 0.5em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-transition" playground>
				<button type="button" class="ui button" commandfor="transition-demo-fade-playground" command="--toggle">Fade up</>
				<button type="button" class="ui button" commandfor="transition-demo-scale-playground" command="--toggle">Scale</>
				<button type="button" class="ui button" commandfor="transition-demo-flip-playground" command="--toggle">Horizontal flip</>
				<ui-stack class="ui-cluster">
					<ui-transition id="transition-demo-fade-playground" animation="fade up" inline visible>
						<ui-segment>Fade up</>
					</>
					<ui-transition id="transition-demo-scale-playground" animation="scale" inline visible>
						<ui-segment>Scale</>
					</>
					<ui-transition id="transition-demo-flip-playground" animation="horizontal flip" duration="500" inline visible>
						<ui-segment>Horizontal flip</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>A theme leaves the animations as they are, and changes the page around them.</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
